        <dg:chunk dg:structure="lim" dg:origin="1 262 3133 294 3172">2.</dg:chunk> Capital Expenditure (CapEx) Analysis</dg:chunk>
      <dg:AnnualCapExReserve dg:structure="p" dg:origin="2 262 260 2205 291; 2 262 306 2091 338; 2 262 353 1587 385" dg:style="color: darkslategray">Due to the aggressive mechanical wear associated with deep-water chemical interactions at the hydrothermal rifts, the annual CapEx sinking reserve is modeled at <dg:chunk dg:structure="span" xsi:type="decimal" dg:value="4.5" dg:origin="2 569 306 640 338">4.5%</dg:chunk> of total revenues, as compared to the typical <dg:chunk dg:structure="span" xsi:type="decimal" dg:value="2.0" dg:origin="2 1271 306 1342 338">2.0%</dg:chunk> standard for lunar or orbital properties. This allocation supports preventative maintenance of the heat exchangers without disrupting cash flow stability.</dg:AnnualCapExReserve>
      <docset:ValuationSummaryAndParameters dg:structure="p" dg:origin="2 262 719 2200 750; 2 262 766 1056 797" dg:style="color: darkslategray" xml:id="valuationsummaryandparameters" dg:itemprop="references" dg:href="#underwritingbasevalue-2">Valuation Conclusion: The collateral property displays robust asset health. The LTV of <docset:UnderwritingBaseValue xsi:type="decimal" dg:value="64.93" dg:origin="2 1486 719 1592 750">64.93%</docset:UnderwritingBaseValue> provides adequate security cushion against extreme tectonic events or regulatory alignment changes.</docset:ValuationSummaryAndParameters>
